give you a strong WR base. The roster export shows Hockenson starting, Andrews and Strange both on the bench, while Ladd is occupying the flex. fileciteturn0file0L11-L16\n\nOn the Seattle backfield, I would **not dump Emanuel Wilson yet**. Week 2 usage actually strengthened his stash case: Wilson played 29 snaps with 21 carries, while Price played 24 snaps with 13 carries before leaving with the shoulder issue. The usage report specifically had Wilson operating as Seattle's No. 2 ahead of George Holani. citeturn283963news2turn283963news30 So because you own Price, Wilson is a legitimate handcuff — not just random bench clutter.\n\nThat gives me this hierarchy right now:\n\n- **Cook:** locked.\n- **Price:** hold/startable, but definitely hasn't broken out yet.\n- **Emanuel Wilson:** hold for the moment because he's directly tied to Price and has real workload evidence.\n- **MarShawn Lloyd / Kyle Monangai:** upside stashes; we need to compare them against whatever is on waivers before cutting either.\n- **Pierce:** perfect IR stash; costs us basically nothing while eligible.\n- **Three TEs:** this is where the roster is inefficient. Hockenson + Andrews + Strange is too much unless we're actively waiting for one of them to pop or using one as trade bait. fileciteturn0file0L13-L16\n\nAnd **Ladd is the frustrating one**. You're getting crushed because the roster construction says that flex spot should be one of your advantages, and right now it isn't. But I don't want us rage-dropping or selling McConkey at the bottom. This is exactly the kind of early-season player where we need to look at **targets, routes, snap share, separation/usage and Herbert's distribution**, not just fantasy points. There was already a preseason case for a 2026 rebound, so two ugly weeks alone aren't enough for me to declare the asset broken. citeturn283963news5\n\nOne correction from what I said before: **Wilson is probably *less* expendable than Strange.** If we find something juicy on waivers, my first roster-pressure point is likely that third TE, not the Price handcuff.\n\nSo when you show me the waiver wire, we're hunting three things simultaneously: **a TE who can actually become a weekly answer, a WR/RB breakout who can eventually knock Ladd out of the flex, and any high-upside stash that is worth sacrificing Strange for.**\n\nThis team doesn't need a rebuild. It needs us to **turn two or three dead-ish roster slots into live bullets.**", "text_chars": 2648, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "20deed90-d5b1-4958-a9fa-5e479269fd83", "role": "user", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790284939.685, "updated_at": 1790284963.234289, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "here is waiver for RB  ", "text_chars": 23, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": null, "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "ac229d1e-bd05-4c9d-a09e-2ceee9c46c5a", "role": "tool", "role_name": "api_tool", "created_at": 1790284940.391193, "updated_at": 1790284940.391193, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 0, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "tether_browsing_display", "part_kinds": [], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "5c012630-f2bf-47f3-aa0f-0b35ffc001cf", "role": "tool", "role_name": "api_tool", "created_at": 1790284940.682949, "updated_at": 1790284940.682949, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "multimodal_text", "part_kinds": ["text", "text"], "text": "Make sure to include fileciteturn1file0L5-L8 in your response to 