t": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": ["text"]}, {"message_id": "cc32ecea-7754-4ff3-8130-d39ace202684", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790284946.2592, "updated_at": 1790284946.2592, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "thoughts", "part_kinds": [], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "89507a26-9500-40e5-b31e-0e9f07f0b1b6", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790284946.332069, "updated_at": 1790284946.332069, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "reasoning_recap", "part_kinds": [], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "68e92349-c2d1-4529-b63d-46ee8882efa6", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790284946.397449, "updated_at": 1790284962.724215, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "Yep — this is exactly the kind of RB waiver pool I wanted to see. And **I would not dump Emanuel Wilson for most of these guys**. He’s actually one of the hotter Week 3 waiver adds league-wide right now. citeturn732193search16turn732193search17\n\nFrom *your actual available list*, the names that matter are **Emmett Johnson, Braelon Allen, Kamara, Kaleb Johnson, and maybe Singleton as a pure upside lottery ticket**. Your export confirms all of them are sitting there as free agents. fileciteturn1file0L3-L11 fileciteturn1file0L21-L26\n\nMy order **for your roster specifically** would be:\n\n1. **Emmett Johnson** — this is my favorite stash on that screen. He was already identified in preseason as the KC RB2 to target, and he’s now a recommended Week 3 add in 10-team formats. That’s exactly your style: cheap bench player whose value can explode if the backfield changes. citeturn732193news10turn732193search17  \n2. **Braelon Allen** — another legit contingency/upside back, not just filler. He’s still being recommended in 12-team leagues. citeturn732193search17  \n3. **Alvin Kamara** — interesting name, but much more floor than lottery-ticket ceiling at this stage. Current waiver guidance actually has him below the explosive contingency backs. citeturn732193search17  \n4. **Kaleb Johnson** — deeper speculative add. The market is moving toward him, but he’s still more “stash and see” than immediate answer. citeturn732193search16turn732193search17  \n5. **Nicholas Singleton** — I still like the *idea* of the rookie, especially since we already talked about him, but right now the NFL opportunity isn’t showing up enough to make me sacrifice a stronger live stash. Yahoo has him only 2% rostered on this wire. fileciteturn1file0L22-L22\n\nThe important part: **Emanuel Wilson stays ahead of most of these.** Week 3 waiver tracking has him as the single biggest RB ownership riser in one dataset, and RotoBaller has him as an add in 10-team leagues. citeturn732193search16turn732193search17 So I retract the earlier thought that Wilson might be our easy cut.\n\nWhat I’d do right now is **hold Cook / Price / Wilson / Lloyd / Monangai**. The only RB waiver guy I’m seriously tempted to force onto this roster is **Emmett Johnson**. If we decide to add him, I’d rather create the slot by cutting **Brenton Strange** from that ridiculous third-TE pile than sacrificing one of these upside RBs.\n\nAnd there’s one important wrinkle: **Kaelon Black is not actually available yet** — Yahoo shows him on waivers until September 25 — and he’s ranked even higher than Emmett by some current waiver sources. fileciteturn1file0L9-L9 citeturn732193search17 So I’d keep an eye on him too.\n\n**Current Don RB bench philosophy:** don’t collect boring RB4s. Keep backs who can become an RB2 overnight.\n\nNext, send me the **WR waiver list**. That’s where I think we may find the more important move, because we need somebody who can start pressuring Ladd’s flex slot.", "text_chars": 2992, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "c6e89a18-939b-41a5-b844-917edfe028d6", "role": "user", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790284994.104, "updated_at": 1790285010.151398, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "Yeah, I was looking at Allen. The thing is, is should we dump Strange and stash another running back from the tight end pool, or fucking Andrews? I— we gotta ride with— we gotta dump Andrews or Strange for— and stash a running back. I think ", "text_chars": 241, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": null, "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "781c1f42-f1df-4190-aa22-6b2b26dc1f13", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790284997.493982, "updated_at": 1790284997.493982, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "web.run", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": ["text"]}, {"message_id": "ccbf41de-c5bf-45b7-8a1b-1741ed2274e7", "role": "tool", "role_name": "web.run", "created_at": 1790284997.595404, "updated_at": 1790284997.595404, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": ["text"]}, {"message_id": "baa2851d-3cef-4b88-a5e8-c8518745dc71", "role": "tool", "role_name": "web.run", "created_at": 1790284998.66253, "updated_at": 1790284998.66253, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": ["text"]}, {"message_id": "5d2fefb1-6f24-47e6-917f-b017183d2cce", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790284999.286722, "updated_at": 1790284999.286722, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "thoughts", "part_kinds": [], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "8a079a7e-01b9-4856-bb50-29b220727407", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790284999.291932, "updated_at": 1790284999.291932, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "reasoning_recap", "part_kinds": [], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "f38dc5fb-ce69-4332-87dd-653ebd5726da", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790284999.294483, "updated_at": 1790285009.716684, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "**I think you’re right: one of the three TEs needs to become another RB lottery ticket.** And between Andrews and Strange, **I’d cut Strange first and keep Andrews.**\n\nThe reason is usage, not name value. Through two games, Andrews has a **23.2% target share, 30% first-read share, 67.6% route share, and 2.13 yards per route run**. That’s still strong underlying TE usage despite the mediocre fantasy output so far. citeturn829033news3turn829033news8 Strange, meanwhile, is sitting at just a **9.6% target share and 10.5% first-read share**, and current Week 3 analysis has him only TE23 in points per game. citeturn829033news9\n\nSo your TE room should become:\n\n**Hockenson — ride him for now.**  \n**Andrews — hold as the second bullet / rebound asset.**  \n**Strange — expendable.**\n\nThen I’d turn Strange into **Braelon Allen or Emmett Johnson**. Both are available in your league; Allen is only 17% rostered and Emmett 32%. fileciteturn1file0L6-L7\n\nAnd knowing how you like to construct these benches, I actually like **Allen** a lot for you. You’re not looking for somebody who gives you 5.8 points when Price has a bad week. You want somebody sitting there who can suddenly become **a serious starting RB if the depth chart breaks his way**.\n\nSo I’d make the move:\n\n**DROP Brenton Strange → ADD Braelon Allen.**\n\nThen your RB stable becomes **Cook / Price / Lloyd / Monangai / Emanuel Wilson / Braelon Allen**, with Pierce occupying IR. That is a much better use of the roster slot than carrying three TEs. Your current roster confirms Strange is just sitting behind Hockenson and Andrews anyway. fileciteturn0file0L13-L20\n\nI would **not cut Andrews yet**. His box scores are annoying, but the underlying workload says there’s still something there. Strange is the redundant piece.", "text_chars": 1800, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "d22b72de-8944-4696-b3fd-c118419bf87e", "role": "user", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790285037.493, "updated_at": 1790285055.079258, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "Yeah, I agree, I agree. We're gonna ride Hockenson. Hockenson came back after 2 years. See, here's the thing though. I'd rather ride with— so Allen has decent upsides, but Emmitt Johnson's going to get more carries, and they're beating the shit out of Kenneth Walker, and he was a little banged up in the preseason, I think. They're gonna have to relieve Kenneth Walker. He's fucking been a monster. In KC. I'd rather either stash the kid— no, you're right. ", "text_chars": 458, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": null, "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "598065b0-883e-403f-8c4a-87426ccb51b0", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790285043.794142, "updated_at": 1790285043.794142, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "web.run", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": ["text"]}, {"message_id": "50ad938c-cadb-425f-848d-f929fe15f901", "role": "tool", "role_name": "web.run", "created_at": 1790285043.901456, "updated_at": 1790285043.901456, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": ["text"]}, {"message_id": "a42dd082-ccee-4b4a-b289-d3c396a6f0fd", "role": "tool", "role_name": "web.run", "created_at": 1790285045.087403, "updated_at": 1790285045.087403, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": ["text"]}, {"message_id": "c7ffda5d-9b71-4248-aaeb-d59d9deae744", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790285045.844055, "updated_at": 1790285045.844055, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "thoughts", "part_kinds": [], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "53d5b727-a943-467e-b748-a8af40438e1b", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790285045.851164, "updated_at": 1790285045.851164, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "reasoning_recap", "part_kinds": [], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "0bedda6c-a89b-493b-be72-23e7addba7fd", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790285045.854221, "updated_at": 1790285054.780443, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "Yeah — **you were onto the right thing with Emmett Johnson**.\n\nI checked the current KC situation, and Andy Reid has already said he wants to **increase Emmett Johnson’s snaps specifically to take some load off Kenneth Walker**. Walker has been getting an absurd workload — about **28 touches per game through two weeks** — while Johnson has already flashed with **14 touches for 103 scrimmage yards**. citeturn912928news1turn912928news55\n\nThat changes my preference a little.\n\n## For *your* roster, I’d go:\n**1. Emmett Johnson**  \n**2. Braelon Allen**\n\nAllen may have the cleaner “starter gets hurt and I explode” profile, but Emmett has **two paths to value**:\n\n- his role can grow **without** a Walker injury;\n- if Walker misses time, Emmett’s value could jump massively.\n\nReid literally said he expects Emmett to “continue to get more snaps” as they try to balance the workload. citeturn912928news1\n\nAnd Walker has been ridiculous — **290 rushing yards plus 79 receiving yards through two games** — so KC has every reason to avoid running him into the ground. citeturn912928news1\n\nSo I’d revise the move to:\n\n**DROP Brenton Strange → ADD Emmett Johnson.**\n\nThen we **watch Braelon Allen like a hawk**. If another expendable slot emerges, he’s exactly the next kind of stash I want.\n\nAnd the beautiful part is this gives your bench different kinds of RB upside instead of duplicating bets:\n\n**Cook** = anchor  \n**Price** = current RB2 bet  \n**Wilson** = Price/Seattle contingency value  \n**Lloyd** = breakout stash  \n**Monangai** = Chicago upside stash  \n**Emmett Johnson** = growing KC role + injury-away ceiling\n\nThat’s a much nastier bench than carrying three fucking tight ends.", "text_chars": 1695, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "0467cc78-481d-4862-84fb-7abd160b5246", "role": "user", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790285079.463, "updated_at": 1790285099.111732, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "Yeah, again, but we gotta look at it because Singleton too is prime. Pollard is beat up in fucking Tennessee, and even his— even in the second RB too is beat up in Tennessee. Spears. But that's too much of a committee. I don't like getting involved in committee, especially in a league like this. ", "text_chars": 297, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": null, "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "7884c65c-81e8-4c5b-9ec5-71f0a72abe0d", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790285081.397444, "updated_at": 1790285083.139913, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "Exactly — **that’s the right filter for this league**. We don’t need another “maybe 6 touches, maybe 11 touches” back clogging the bench; we want a stash with a credible path to becoming a real starter. I’m checking the Tennessee depth-chart/injury picture against Emmett and Allen, because that’s the only way Singleton deserves the slot.", "text_chars": 339, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "c3fcf892-a2db-4eba-bff9-dfae5e5b1cdb", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790285084.10356, "updated_at": 1790285084.10356, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "web.run", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": ["text"]}, {"message_id": "83704be0-b1da-400a-b3c4-55de80a4fb23", "role": "tool", "role_name": "web.run", "created_at": 1790285084.204349, "updated_at": 1790285084.204349, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": ["text"]}, {"message_id": "a2dedbb8-f017-4f65-996c-a806a3623bd3", "role": "tool", "role_name": "web.run", "created_at": 1790285085.525308, "updated_at": 1790285085.525308, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": ["text"]}, {"message_id": "c1559459-66dc-4aac-9021-bf61dc341f56", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790285087.070849, "updated_at": 1790285087.070849, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "thoughts", "part_kinds": [], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "81924d7d-5d45-4a66-9245-d020075e7555", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790285087.077694, "updated_at": 1790285087.077694, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "reasoning_recap", "part_kinds": [], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "47a65558-4700-49ab-8c92-4275ae2a26f0", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790285087.080311, "updated_at": 1790285098.659235, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "Yep — **that’s exactly why Singleton is tempting but still third for me.**\n\nTennessee’s situation is legitimately interesting right now: **both Tony Pollard and Tyjae Spears missed Wednesday practice with ankle issues**, and Singleton is the next man up. He finally got four carries in Week 2, so there is a real injury-driven path to touches. citeturn437382news0turn437382news1turn437382news3\n\nBut your committee concern is the key distinction. If Pollard and Spears are active, Singleton can disappear. And even if one misses time, Tennessee’s run blocking has been poor, so you’re betting on both **opportunity opening up and the offense supporting it**. citeturn437382news1\n\nThat’s why I’d rank the stashes for **this roster**:\n\n1. **Emmett Johnson** — best combination of *role already growing + contingency upside*. Andy Reid has explicitly said Johnson will get more snaps to lighten Kenneth Walker’s workload, and Johnson has produced 103 scrimmage yards on only 14 touches. citeturn437382news19turn437382news10\n2. **Braelon Allen** — cleaner classic lottery ticket. His independent role isn’t huge, but if the backfield opens, he has the body/TD profile to become useful fast. He already scored in Week 2. citeturn437382news21\n3. **Nicholas Singleton** — arguably the most explosive speculative bet, but the current path is messier because Pollard + Spears are both ahead of him when healthy.\n\nAnd Singleton is just **2% rostered** in your Yahoo league, so we probably don’t need to panic-grab him this second. fileciteturn1file0L22-L22\n\nSo I still like:\n\n**Strange → Emmett Johnson.**\n\nThen we watch Singleton very closely through the rest of this week. If Pollard and/or Spears trend toward being out, **Singleton immediately moves way up the board**. If both are cleared, I’d rather let somebody else occupy the Tennessee committee headache.\n\nYour instinct is right: **in a shallow/redraft bench, chase pathways to 15+ touches, not permanent 7-touch committee roles.**", "text_chars": 1999, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "31fa1171-5b35-4c4a-8744-1ba89679f264", "role": "user", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790285136.413, "updated_at": 1790285163.282696, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "Here, here's the tight ends. I think we may go Walker in both. Fucking— he's had a huge  and wr pool waivers to review overall -  He's had the huge 2 games, and with a guy like Bryce Young throwing the ball, I don't know who's in Carolina, but a good tight end that they rely on, definitely over Strange. ", "text_chars": 305, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": null, "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "0b11a369-d9bd-43e0-9f54-0792b0741e35", "role": "tool", "role_name": "api_tool", "created_at": 1790285137.244343, "updated_at": 1790285137.244343, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 0, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "tether_browsing_display", "part_kinds": [], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "1992b9b2-4274-43ab-a07a-150e0947672c", "role": "tool", "role_name": "api_tool", "created_at": 1790285137.715975, "updated_at": 1790285137.715975, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "multimodal_text", "part_kinds": ["text", "text"], "text": "Make sure to include fileciteturn2file0L5-L8 in your response to cite this file, or to surface it as a link. Replace the placeholder line range with the actual line range from the result that best fits the snippet you want to surface with the citation. If you cite multiple files, use a separate complete `filecite` marker for each file. Never put multiple `turnNfileM` targets inside a single `filecite` marker.\nUse ref_id \"turn2file0\" to reference this file. For broad questions