nt": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "I’d **wait one more week on Andrews unless we need the roster spot right now**.\n\nThe reason is that Andrews’ box score has been mediocre, but his underlying usage is still strong: through two games he has a **23.2% target share, 30% first-read share, 67.6% route participation and 2.13 yards per route run**. That’s not a dead TE profile. citeturn879631news8\n\nAt the same time, **Emmett Johnson is the stash I like most if we do make the move**. Andy Reid has already said Johnson’s snaps are going up to reduce Kenneth Walker’s workload, and Walker has an absurd **56 touches through two games**. Johnson has also been productive on limited work. citeturn879631news11\n\nSo my current move order is:\n\n- **Drop Strange first**, no hesitation.\n- **Add Worthy** if he’s still free.\n- Next open slot: **Emmett Johnson**.\n- **Hold Andrews through this week** unless we need his slot to secure Emmett now.\n- If Andrews gives us another dud despite that strong usage, then next week I’m much more comfortable turning him into another RB stash.\n\nFor the bench, I’d rather have **Hockenson + Andrews + a pile of upside RBs** than Hockenson + Waller + Andrews. We already have Hockenson as the guy we’re riding. The second TE should either have genuine trade/ceiling value or vacate the slot.\n\nSo if you’re asking me **“Andrews → Emmett Johnson today, yes or no?”** my answer is: **only if Emmett looks like he’s going to get scooped. Otherwise hold Andrews one more game and reassess.**", "text_chars": 1482, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "1cbd15ee-8725-4ba7-a65f-84cdfb3c4c81", "role": "user", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790285272.492, "updated_at": 1790285299.369149, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text"