": null, "created_at": 1790285286.492557, "updated_at": 1790285286.492557, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "reasoning_recap", "part_kinds": [], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "49cd0409-9091-4e88-bafb-08785d8ea483", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790285286.494833, "updated_at": 1790285298.793916, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "Yeah — **now that I see the updated lineup, the first drop candidate is not Andrews. It’s MarShawn Lloyd.**\n\nYour bench is currently **Andrews, Higgins, Lloyd, Monangai, Emanuel Wilson, Waller**, with Pierce safely parked on IR. fileciteturn3file0L9-L15\n\nHere’s why Lloyd has moved to the front of the cut line: through two weeks he’s averaging only **10.5 touches and 31.5 yards**, played just 28% of the snaps last week, and Green Bay has turned into a three-man backfield with Chris Brooks and Kaleb Johnson. Lloyd also lost a fumble in Week 2 and didn’t get another touch afterward. Current analysis explicitly has him trending *away* from the lead role. citeturn428471news20turn428471news22\n\nMeanwhile, **Monangai is absolutely not a drop**. He’s averaging 12 touches and 91 total yards, has been extremely efficient, and currently sits RB17 in fantasy points per game despite a sub-40% snap share. He does have a knee issue we need to monitor, but the actual football usage says hold. citeturn428471news28turn428471news29\n\nAndrews also stays for now. His underlying numbers remain strong — **23.2% target share, 30% first-read share, 2.13 YPRR** — and he gets Dallas, which has been very favorable to TEs. citeturn428471news31 Waller is the upside TE experiment; Hockenson is the guy you’re riding.\n\nSo my current **drop ladder** is:\n\n1. **MarShawn Lloyd**\n2. **Emanuel Wilson**, depending on Seattle/Price usage\n3. **Darren Waller**, if the Carolina role proves touchdown-dependent\n4. **Mark Andrews**, only if his usage collapses rather than just his box score\n5. **Nobody else**\n\nLadd is nowhere near this conversation. He’s starting in your flex and still 98% rostered. fileciteturn3file0L8-L8 And Higgins definitely stays; he’s basically luxury depth right now. fileciteturn3file0L10-L10\n\nSo if **Emmett Johnson is still free**, I actually like **Lloyd → Emmett Johnson** more than Andrews → Emmett.\n\nThat lets us keep all three TE shots for one more week **without sacrificing the better RB stashes**.", "text_chars": 2036, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "374dc809-e7cf-4fd8-bcb2-d55d06d0e7f7", "role": "user", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790285318.468, "updated_at": 1790285332.018375, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "Yeah, I know. Yeah, I agree. Lloyd could go. I thought Lloyd— it's too much of a clusterfuck. So who do you want to drop Lloyd for? Go with the kid from Kansas City. I agree, let's get rid of Lloyd. ", "text_chars": 199, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": null, "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "67201436-3953-4992-a004-ceab20065144", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790285325.210673, "updated_at": 1790285325.210673, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "web.run", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": ["text"]}, {"message_id": "8930a81e-ca9f-4baa-82cc-a08af1e468c1", "role": "tool", "role_name": "web.run", "created_at": 1790285325.31206, "updated_at": 1790285325.31206, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": ["text"]}, {"message_id": "2e718b97-4870-4527-8a82-4757b718dfb8", "role": "tool", "role_name": "web.run", "created_at": 1790285326.357925, "updated_at": 1790285326.357925, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": ["text"]}, {"message_id": "8e6eb217-550c-4fa8-8855-fa84dd5ab952", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790285326.765792, "updated_at": 1790285326.765792, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "thoughts", "part_kinds": [], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "d6419496-6616-45c7-9f5e-1eac51cd37b6", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790285326.771843, "updated_at": 1790285326.771843, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "reasoning_recap", "part_kinds": [], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "0b88c956-84a2-4220-a250-fd0620064167", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790285326.77494, "updated_at": 1790285331.553536, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "Yep. **Lloyd → Emmett Johnson. That’s the move I’d make.**\n\nYou’re giving up a messy Green Bay committee for a rookie whose arrow is actively pointing up. Andy Reid said Emmett will **“continue to get more snaps”** specifically to take some of the workload off Kenneth Walker, and Johnson already has **103 scrimmage yards on just 14 touches**. citeturn751467news0turn751467news4\n\nThat fits your bench philosophy much better: **not a guy we need to start now, but a guy whose role can grow organically and who has huge contingent upside if Walker misses time.**\n\nSo the move is:\n\n**DROP MarShawn Lloyd**  \n**ADD Emmett Johnson**\n\nThen we leave the rest alone for now and reassess Andrews/Waller after this week.", "text_chars": 715, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}], "ordering_is_monotonic": true, "total_text_chars": 378958, "code_block_count": 0, "link_count": 729, "citation_count": 729, "path_reference_count": 0, "model_slugs": ["gpt-5-6-thinking"], "unextractable_part_kinds": ["text"], "capture": {"capture_status": "ok", "captured_at": "2026-09-26T08:38:56Z", "capture_path": null, "pages_walked": 1, "content_types": ["model_editable_context", "multimodal_text", "reasoning_recap", "tether_browsing_display", "text", "thoughts"], "warnings": []}, "provenance": {"observation_id": "9c498615d03643058fbda325ba795235", "source_artifact_path": "C:\\Users\\Dekan AI Brother\\Projects\\ACTIVE\\gce-ingestion-w1\\store\\chatgpt-backup\\EVIDENCE\\blobs\\sha256\\76\\76cb4e540154e7b48a11f75cc22db1f958daafbcd49d34f2695e2293fd09f4f9", "source_content_hash": "76cb4e540154e7b48a11f75cc22db1f958daafbcd4